    "created_at": "2022-03-02T22:43:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-02T22:43:12Z",
    "body": "> I think they should continue to be `false`. If you start allowing quotation marks you make the _features_ tokenizer more complicated, at least if you want it to make sense, e.g.:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> noopener=\", popup=1, \"\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> Does this have `popup=1` as a feature, or no?\r\n\r\nRight - that's a great point. Ok, I agree with you, quotes should parse as false.\r\n\r\nOk, quick and dirty tests have been added here: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/33029 \r\nComments appreciated. I will wait to land them until I've sent an intent to ship for Chromium, and the spec has landed.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
